WF-30 — Payment Pending Intent Filter

## Summary

- Inputs (WF-01 canonical envelope per data-contract-discipline Phase 1 — design.md §2.1): `phoneNumber` (E.164 string), `messageType`, `messageContent`, `user` (object: {id, phone_number, name, status, slack_channel_id, current_consultation_id}), `pendingUser` (null for payment_pending users). Additional fields passed by WF-02: `messageText`, `userId`, `userStatus`.
- Outputs: For `general_enquiry` intent — a Gemini-generated WhatsApp reply tailored to the payment-pending stage. For other pass-through intents — a contextual WhatsApp payment reminder. For stop_intent — a stop-intent clarifier message. On Gemini General Response outage — sends user apology + dual admin alerts then halts via stopAndError (error propagates to WF-02 caller).
- State Transitions: none. Auto-opt-out on Gemini-classified stop_intent removed 2026-05-23 (SP-04); explicit STOP keyword via WF-20 still unsubscribes canonically.
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-25 (Intent Classifier), WF-50 (Send WhatsApp), WF-51 (Send Slack Message — admin alerts on Gemini outage).
- **Notes:**
  - **General-enquiry Gemini branch (2026-05-26 — GAP-3C):** `general_enquiry` intent now routes to a Gemini-generated contextual reply with a payment-pending stage cue (gentle nudge to complete the ₹500 payment) and an email-callout (`chinmay_astro@gmail.com`). Other pass-through intents (wants_consultation, rebook_intent, feedback_intent) keep the existing canned payment-reminder reply.
  - **Gemini General Response halt-and-notify (2026-05-27 — TD-PGF-09 scope expansion):** Identical pattern to WF-23. Gemini outage on `Gemini General Response` no longer silently halts the workflow. The HTTP node has `onError=continueErrorOutput`; on retries exhausted (3× with backoff), the error branch fans out to user apology (WF-50) + dual admin alerts (WF-51 to user's consult channel + admin-commands), then a `stopAndError` node terminates execution. The error propagates to WF-02's `Call WF-30` executeWorkflow node which halts the caller. Admin alert text: "AI assistant couldn't generate a reply" (General Response variant). Payment-pending users have a consult Slack channel (created at form submission per Design Rule #2) — both consult-channel AND admin-commands alerts will fire. User-apology + admin-alert copy locked 2026-05-27T02:25:00Z.
  - **stop_intent policy (2026-05-23 — SP-04, applying WF-40's TD-E pattern):** Gemini-classified stop_intent no longer auto-routes to WF-47 unsubscribe — false-positive risk (e.g. user typing "I want to stop waiting for confirmation"). Instead WF-30 sends a clarifier asking the user to send STOP exactly. Literal STOP still flows through WF-20 (Design Rule #5).
  - For intents in {garbage, malicious_abusive, inappropriate}, WF-25 already handles the response internally and does NOT return to caller — those messages terminate inside WF-25.
  - **`Is Pass-Through Intent?` IF simplified 2026-05-27 (TD-PGF-05):** Previously tested 4 intent types ({garbage, malicious_abusive, inappropriate, stop_intent}) all combined with notEquals + AND. After the WF-25 halt-inside-WF-25 redesign (TD-PGF-09), garbage/malicious_abusive/inappropriate never return to caller — they terminate inside WF-25. Only `stop_intent` is reachable as a non-pass-through value. IF now has a single condition testing `intentResult != "stop_intent"`. Semantics preserved: TRUE branch = pass-through path; FALSE branch = stop_intent path.
  - **Call WF-25 envelope add-on (2026-05-27 — TD-PGF-05):** caller-side `workflowInputs.value` mapping extended from 4 fields (phoneNumber, userId, messageText, userStatus) to 6 fields, adding `userName` (from `user.name`) and `slackChannelId` (from `user.slack_channel_id`) per data-contract-discipline. Payment-pending users always have user populated (Design Rule #2 — channel created at form submission), so no null-guard fallback needed here — but `(... || {}).field` is still used defensively in case envelope shape varies.
  - WF-25 caller field name (TD-DRIFT-009): passes `messageText` but WF-25 reads `messageContent` — explicitly deferred from Phase 1 per §1.5.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — Triggered by parent workflow with WF-01 canonical envelope plus {messageText, userId, userStatus}. Read `phoneNumber` from top-level envelope field (canonical per §2.1).
Step 2: Call WF-25 with 6 fields: phoneNumber, userId, messageText, userStatus, userName (from `user.name`), slackChannelId (from `user.slack_channel_id`). Receive intentResult. Note: WF-25 may itself halt-and-notify on its own Gemini outage; that halt propagates here and on to WF-02.
Step 3: Check `Is Pass-Through Intent?` — is intentResult != "stop_intent"? (simplified single-condition IF per TD-PGF-05 dead-branch cleanup)
  - If YES (pass-through — wants_consultation, general_enquiry, rebook_intent, feedback_intent) → GOTO Step 4
  - If NO (stop_intent — only reachable non-pass-through per WF-25 contract) → GOTO Step 19
Step 4: Check `Is General Enquiry?` — is intentResult == "general_enquiry"?
  - If YES → GOTO Step 5
  - If NO → GOTO Step 17
Step 5: Build Gemini prompt instructing a helpful, warm assistant for Chinmay's Vedic astrology consultation service on WhatsApp, with the user-stage cue "user has completed the intake form but has not yet paid the ₹500 consultation fee" and the email-callout cue "they can email chinmay_astro@gmail.com for anything else". Ask Gemini to weave both naturally into a brief 2-3 sentence reply in plain conversational English (no bullet lists, no robotic phrasing). Append the user's messageContent.
Step 6: POST to Gemini (gemini-2.5-flash-lite per project standard) with temperature=0.3, maxOutputTokens=200, timeout=10s, retryOnFail=true, maxTries=3, onError=continueErrorOutput. On success (main output): GOTO Step 7. On retries exhausted (error output): GOTO Step 8 (halt-and-notify chain).
Step 7: Extract Gemini reply text from candidates[0].content.parts[0].text; fallback default "Thank you for your message! For questions about our Vedic astrology consultation, feel free to ask." Call WF-50 with { phoneNumber, messageType="text", messageContent=reply } per §2.3 canonical contract. End.
Step 8: Build user apology WF-50 payload per §2.3 — { phoneNumber, messageType="text", messageContent="Sorry — we ran into a brief technical issue and couldn't process your message just now. Dr. Chinmay has been notified and will follow up with you shortly. We apologise for the inconvenience." }.
Step 9: Call WF-50 (apology to user). Continue to admin alert chain (Step 10).
Step 10: Build admin alert text (Code node) — translate userStatus to plain English (payment_pending → "awaiting payment approval"; etc.). Resolve userName. Construct messageText: "⚠️ The AI assistant couldn't generate a reply to a user just now.\n\n*User:* {userName} ({phoneNumber})\n*Their state:* {stateText}\n*Their question:* \"{messageContent truncated to 500 chars}\"\n*Reason:* {error summary truncated to 200 chars}\n\nThe user has been told there's a technical hiccup and that you'll follow up. Suggested action: respond manually in their consult channel." Emit { messageText }.
Step 11: Check `Has Consult Channel?` — is `user.slack_channel_id` non-empty (notEmpty unary)?
  - If YES → GOTO Step 12 (consult-channel alert path, then admin-commands alert).
  - If NO → GOTO Step 14 (admin-commands alert only — should be unreachable for payment_pending users but defensive).
Step 12: Build consult alert payload per §2.5 — { channelId: `user.slack_channel_id`, messageText: `$('Build Admin Alert Text').item.json.messageText` }.
Step 13: Call WF-51 (consult-channel alert). GOTO Step 14.
Step 14: Build admin-commands alert payload per §2.5 — { channelId: "C0A5B0ZE81E", messageText: `$('Build Admin Alert Text').item.json.messageText` }.
Step 15: Call WF-51 (admin-commands alert). GOTO Step 16.
Step 16: stopAndError — terminate WF-30 execution with errorMessage "Gemini general response failed; user apology + admin alerts dispatched. Halting execution so caller propagates termination." n8n's executeWorkflow error-propagation contract halts WF-02 at its `Call WF-30` node.
Step 17: (pass-through non-general-enquiry path — from Step 4 NO branch) Build contextual payment reminder message:
  - If intentResult == "wants_consultation": prefix "Great! You're almost there. To confirm your consultation, please complete the payment below."
  - Else if intentResult == "rebook_intent": prefix "For rebooking, please complete the pending payment first."
  - Else: prefix "Happy to help! Once your payment is confirmed, Chinmay will be ready for your consultation."
  - Append UPI block: ₹500 to +91-9653240263 (Chinmay Mujumdar), then "tap the Payment Completed button you received earlier."
Step 18: Call WF-50 with { phoneNumber, messageType="text", messageContent=assembled message } per §2.3 canonical contract. End.
Step 19: (stop_intent path — from Step 3 NO branch) Build WF-50 stop-intent clarifier payload per §2.3 canonical contract:
  - phoneNumber = <phoneNumber> (from top-level envelope)
  - messageType = "text"
  - messageContent = "This is an automated message from Chinmay Astro — we noticed your message mentioned STOP or unsubscribing. If this was unrelated, please ignore. If you do want to opt out of this service, simply send STOP at any time."
Step 20: Call WF-50 (Stop Clarifier) with the prepared payload. End.
